/-!
# The FF catalogue on the full original local family

The original normalizer action supplies B.5.1 on the subgroup generated by
best offenders. A nontrivial offender forces that subgroup to contain the
same quasisimple component. The source classifier retains all six action
clauses; its group projection uses actual isomorphisms on the literal image.

Every eligible K in L(G₁,S) is covered, even when S permutes K. Original
pre-exclusion and later exchanged-source applications use this same theorem.
The original prime and both exchanged-plane sizes are retained. Larger-field
exclusion, block reconstruction and parabolic clauses remain necessary for
the full 15.1.20--22 catalogue.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 15.1.20(2), pp.1094--1095, and B.5.1, pp.99--103.
-/

public section
